; AI-generated: this file was written by Claude, an AI model.

; The squash of one flap of the folded preliminary base, written as a fan at
; the base's closed corner (ADR 0044). The flap's spine --h & --da opens, and
; --s and --t, one on each layer of the flap, lie on one ray of the table.
; The center line --ac & .a folds in the layer under the flap. The tip does
; not surround the corner, so the fan has no Kawasaki condition there; each
; piece moves by the creases on its paper path, and the piece of the top
; layer under the axis turns by a quarter of a right angle about the corner
; while the piece of the second layer beside it is reflected across the axis.
; The pieces land where the squash of ADR 0038, folded from the flat sheet,
; puts them.

paper square
mark (through .a .c) as --ac
mark (through .b .d) as --bd
mark (map --ab onto --cd) as --h
mark (map --da onto --bc) as --v
mark (align (--h onto --ac) (heading --h)) as --s
mark (align (--h onto --bd) (heading --h)) as --t
.q = free on --ab from .a at 1/4
.r = free on --ab from .b at 1/4
.z = free on --cd from .c at 1/4
.e = free on --da from .d at 1/4
.f = free on --da from .a at 1/4
flatten (--h & --bc) (--v & --cd) (--h & --da) (--v & --ab) (--bd & .b) (--bd & .d) (.q over .r) (toward .q)
flatten (--h & --da) (--s & --da) (--t & --da) (--ac & .a) (on #[.f]) (staying .q)

